      "message": "I\u0027m not sure I fully understand your question, but here\u0027s how it is supposed to work when a retry is necessary:\n\n - The test runs the first time, and this line gets called, telling DeviceConfigRule that the URL should be set to TEST_HTTPS_URL_PATH\n - At some point later, the device syncs flags with the server, and the URL gets overwritten to some other value (or removed)\n - The test continues, and possibly fails on L.189/190 because the captive portal is not detected\n - DeviceConfigRule catches the failure, and checks if the flags were changed. It notices that the HTTPS URL is not TEST_HTTPS_URL_PATH anymore\n - DeviceConfigRule calls base.evaluate() again, which calls setup/test/teardown again\n - Repeat up to retryCountBeforeSIfConfigChanged times\n\nSo I think this should be working: we set the config here, and the config is changed later by some external process (around L.189). If that happens and the test fails, it will be rerun.",
